 'Divergence and Stokes theorems connect local differential laws to integral flux and circulation laws with consistent orientations. Boundary conditions and constitutive relations remain necessary for a field solution. In matter, dispersion and polarization alter wave propagation; the vacuum result is not a universal material light speed.',
